  "h1": "Bluevine Alternatives 2026: Prices and Plans Compared",
  "metaDescription": "Compare Bluevine alternatives for 2026: Mercury, Relay, Novo, Lili, Chase and OnDeck, with published account fees, APY rates and credit terms.",
  "published": "2026-11-18",
  "updated": "2026-11-18",
  "intro": "Mercury, Relay, Novo, Lili and Chase are the five business checking alternatives compared here, and OnDeck is the line-of-credit alternative; Novo, Mercury and Lili Core charge $0 per month, Relay Starter charges $0, and Chase Business Complete Banking charges $15 per month unless waived. At The Modern Wallet, we examine published fee schedules, account minimums and interest rates so business owners can evaluate annual operating costs directly.\n\n[Bluevine](https://www.bluevine.com/) describes itself as a financial technology company, not a bank. Its deposits receive Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) protection up to $3 million per depositor through Coastal Community Bank, Member FDIC, and its sweep program banks. Bluevine Business Checking features three tiers: Standard with no monthly service fee and 1.3% Annual Percentage Yield (APY) up to $250,000 upon meeting activity targets, Plus at $30 per month with 1.75% APY up to $250,000, and Premier at $95 per month with 3.3% APY on all balances. Beyond checking accounts, Bluevine markets an embedded business line of credit up to $250,000 issued by Celtic Bank, alongside partner term loans up to $500,000 and Small Business Administration (SBA) 7(a) loans up to $350,000 through Fundera by NerdWallet.\n\nBecause banking accounts and financing tools serve different jobs, compare the checking options in our [best business bank accounts roundup](/roundup/best-business-bank-accounts/) and research credit terms through our [business line of credit rates by lender guide](/roundup/business-line-of-credit-rates-by-lender/). Readers reviewing borrowing qualification rules can also consult our [business line of credit requirements guide](/guides/business-line-of-credit-requirements/) and the broader [comparison hub](/compare/).",
